---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Particle Physics Cheat Sheet | Free Standard Model, Quarks, Leptons"
  description="Complete particle physics cheat sheet with Standard Model, quarks, and leptons. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Particle Physics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Standard Model, quarks, and leptons. From fundamental particles to forces.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Standard Model</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fundamental Particles</h3>
        <pre><code>Quarks: u, d, c, s, t, b
Leptons: e, μ, τ, ν_e, ν_μ, ν_τ
Gauge bosons: γ, W±, Z, g
Scalar boson: Higgs (H)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Forces</h3>
        <pre><code>Strong: gluon (g), color charge
Weak: W±, Z bosons
Electromagnetic: photon (γ)
Gravity: graviton (hypothetical)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Quarks</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Quark Properties</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Quark</th><th>Charge</th><th>Mass (MeV)</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Up (u)</td><td>+2/3</td><td>2.3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Down (d)</td><td>-1/3</td><td>4.8</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Charm (c)</td><td>+2/3</td><td>1275</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Strange (s)</td><td>-1/3</td><td>95</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Top (t)</td><td>+2/3</td><td>173,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bottom (b)</td><td>-1/3</td><td>4180</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Leptons</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Lepton Properties</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Lepton</th><th>Charge</th><th>Mass (MeV)</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Electron (e)</td><td>-1</td><td>0.511</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Muon (μ)</td><td>-1</td><td>105.7</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tau (τ)</td><td>-1</td><td>1777</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Electron neutrino</td><td>0</td><td>< 2.2 eV</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Muon neutrino</td><td>0</td><td>< 0.17 MeV</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tau neutrino</td><td>0</td><td>< 18.2 MeV</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Conservation Laws</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Conserved Quantities</h3>
        <pre><code>Charge: always conserved
Baryon number: always conserved
Lepton number: always conserved
Strangeness: conserved in strong, not weak
Color: always conserved</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
